.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt PATINA-POLKIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-polkit
.Nd the Patina desktop's polkit agent
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks for your password when an app needs administrator rights:
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
GParted, Disks, Software, and anything else that asks
.Xr polkit 8 .
.Xr patina-compositor 1
keeps it running in the session.
It registers with polkit as the agent for this login session; when polkit
needs a password it shows a dialog in the middle of the screen with what the
app is asking for and who is authenticating, and the password is checked by
polkit's own agent helper.
Escape or Cancel closes the dialog and refuses the request; a wrong password
asks again.
.Pp
polkit allows one agent per session, so
.Nm
stops with an error where there already is one, as in a GNOME session.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.It Fl -ask Fl -user Ar name Fl -message Ar text
The dialog itself, which the agent starts for each request; it speaks the
agent's line protocol on standard input and output, so it isn't useful by
hand.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_SESSION_ID
The login session to register for; without it, logind is asked.
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN
The skin to wear, as the bar sets it; otherwise the bar's config's.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-lock 1 ,
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7 ,
.Xr polkit 8
